---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Thomas Vezzani" description="About Thomas Vezzani, independent software designer and AI systems builder in Brussels.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-intro">
      <div class="kicker">About</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">I build systems around what matters to me.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-photo"><img src="/assets/avatar-real-dither.png" alt="Thomas Vezzani" /></div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p>I am Thomas, an independent software designer, AI systems builder and founder in Brussels. I like simple answers to complex problems, local-first software, strange little interfaces, and tools that give control back to the person using them.</p>
        <p>Outside software I care about music, drawing, film photography, 3D and art in general. Those things leak into the way I think about products, which is probably a good thing.</p>
        <div class="principles">
          <div class="principle"><span>01</span><span><strong>Evidence over theatre.</strong> If an AI does not know, silence or abstention can be the correct feature.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><span>02</span><span><strong>Control is part of UX.</strong> Privacy, local execution and explicit boundaries change how a product feels, not just how it is hosted.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><span>03</span><span><strong>Minimum sufficient sophistication.</strong> I like clever systems; I like deleting unnecessary cleverness more.</span></div>
          <div class="principle"><span>04</span><span><strong>Make the thing tangible.</strong> A working artifact teaches more than a perfect abstract plan.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
